Q: Error when attempting raw INSERT query with $this-&gt;$db-&gt;query($sql) in CodeIgniter A: <p>Why send <code>$_POST</code>? Use <code>$this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;param_name&quot;)</code> and in your instance <code>$this-&gt;load-&gt;model('Contacts_model');</code>.</p>
<p>In my practice, I use <code>$this-&gt;load-&gt;model('Contacts_model', 'instance', [true or false]);</code>. The last parameter is optional (to connect with the DB if you don't use autoload option).</p>
<p>Use this:</p>
<pre><code>function insertContact()
{
    $title = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;title&quot;);
    $f_name = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;f_name&quot;);
    $sql = &quot;INSERT INTO contacts (title,f_name) &quot; .
        &quot;VALUES ('&quot; . $this-&gt;db-&gt;escape($title) . &quot;','&quot;.$this-&gt;db-&gt;escape($f_name) .&quot;')&quot;;
    $this-&gt;$db-&gt;query($sql);
}
</code></pre>
<p>DON'T USE <code>$_POST</code>! (And use the Active Record, read the user guide.)</p>
